WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:12.500
The reproductive cyle begins with ovulation, 
the release of a ripe egg, or ovum, from the ovary

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Hundreds of thousands of follicles 
sit nestled inside the ovary.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Each follicle is a sphere of cells 
with an immature egg at its center.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.800
The typical 28-day menstrual cycle begins
on the first day of menstrual bleeding.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.900
During the first 7 days of the cycle, 
a few follicles start to grow.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:37.000
These maturing follicles secrete estrogen
hormone into the blood stream

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.900
to prepare the lining of 
the uterus for pregnancy.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:48.980
Around Day 7, all of the follicles stop growing
and begin to degenerate except for one.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:55.100
This dominant follicle continues to grow, 
nourishing the developing egg inside it.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:01.300
Around Day 12, the follicle secretes 
a surge of estrogen into the blood stream.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.900
When the estrogen reaches the hypothalamus 
and the pituitary gland in the brain,

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:11.900
the anterior or front part of the pituitary gland
floods the blood stream with luteinizing hormone.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:21.500
Around day 14, luteinizing hormone causes
the follicle to undergo a sudden growth spurt.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:27.900
Right before ovulation, the egg detaches 
from the inside of the follicle.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.600
The bulging follicle releases chemicals,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:38.000
signaling one of the two fallopian tubes 
to move in closer and envelope the follicle.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.200
The follicle swells until... it bursts open,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.000
ejecting the ovum and fluid from 
the follicle into the abdominal cavity.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:55.700
In response, the fimbriae, 
tiny finger-like projections

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:02.700
at the end of the fallopian tube, sweep across
the ovulation site and pick up the ovum.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:08.900
Microscopic cilia on the fimbrial surface
guide the ovum to the entrance of the fallopian tube.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.600
Muscular contractions 
along the wall of the fallopian tube

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.379
gently propel the ovum 
toward the uterus.

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:18.800
The ovum lives for 12-24 hours,

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.600
the interval when fertilization can occur.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.200
If not fertilized, the ovum will disintegrate

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.700
and be shed along with the 
uterine lining during menstruation,

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:35.700
marking the end of one reproductive cycle 
and the beginning of another.

